(ENV-06: the named lookup (LANGUAGE.md:4856, `environment's "NAME"`)
 asserted against a value the tester controls, both unset and set.
 `check-probes.sh` only special-cases a `Ran:` line for a STDIN feed,
 not a leading `VAR=value` -- so the checked block below is the plain,
 no-variable-set run (deterministic: the probe's variable name is
 namespaced so no host environment sets it by accident), and the
 `FOO=bar`-style run is recorded in the second, unchecked block
 beneath it, hand-verified once.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ENV-06.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   value:
)
(Second run, hand-verified, NOT checked by check-probes.sh:
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ENV-06.vox -o p && VF_PROBE_NAMED_LOOKUP=hello123 ./p
 output:
   matched expected value
)
a text called v is environment's "VF_PROBE_NAMED_LOOKUP".
if v is "hello123", print "matched expected value".
otherwise, print "value: {v}".
